`ErrorBoundary.tsx` created. Usage:

```tsx
// Basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback + error hook
<ErrorBoundary
  onError={(err, info) => reportToSentry(err, info)}
  fallback={(error, retry) => (
    <div>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={retry}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Key details:**
- `getDerivedStateFromError` triggers the fallback render; `componentDidCatch` handles logging
- Logs `{ timestamp, message, stack, componentStack }` to console; calls optional `onError` prop for external services (Sentry, Datadog, etc.)
- Component stack only shown in non-production builds
- `retry()` resets state, causing children to remount — if the error was transient, they recover cleanly
